{"unit":2,"items":54,"pass":38,"title":"Unit Test · Unit 2","tracks":{"a21":"Track_2.1.mp3","a24":"Track_2.4.mp3"},"SEGS":{"story":["a21",3.77,null],"n3":["a24",34.25,44.78],"n5":["a24",68.6,84.91]},"html":"\n  <section class=\"stage on\" data-stage=\"Unit Test\">\n    <div class=\"stage-head\">\n      <div class=\"kicker\">Unit 2 &middot; Unit Test</div>\n      <h2>Stories worth telling</h2>\n      <p>Six parts, <b>54 questions</b>, covering everything in Unit 2: vocabulary, grammar, reading, listening, functional language and one integrated part. Answer them all, then press Check. You need <b>38 out of 54</b> to pass. Parts 7 and 8 are your writing and speaking &mdash; they are not marked automatically, but do not skip them. You can take this test as many times as you like.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"task\" data-task data-tid=\"review-u2\">\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 1 · VOCABULARY ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\">Part 1 &middot; Vocabulary &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 1&ndash;12</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the word that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">1</span><span class=\"body\">Nobody was hurt. Everyone managed to&hellip; through a side door.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">disappear</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">escape</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">float</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">2</span><span class=\"body\">The photograph was a&hellip; &mdash; somebody had put two pictures together.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">conclusion</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">coincidence</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">fake</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">3</span><span class=\"body\">The police asked the public to&hellip; the story and keep the emergency line free.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">ignore</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">circulate</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">invent</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">4</span><span class=\"body\">After forty years the scientists reached an uncomfortable&hellip;: the whole thing was false.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">evidence</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">conclusion</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">claim</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Match each verb to the phrase it goes with. Click one on the left, then one on the right.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">5&ndash;9</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"pairbox\">\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"w1\">be</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"w2\">keep</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"w3\">lose</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"w4\">knock</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"l\" data-key=\"w5\">reach</button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"pcol\">\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"w4\" data-short=\"into somebody\">into somebody</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"w1\" data-short=\"stuck\">stuck</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"w5\" data-short=\"a conclusion\">a conclusion</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"w3\" data-short=\"contact\">contact</button>\n            <button class=\"pit\" data-side=\"r\" data-key=\"w2\" data-short=\"quiet\">quiet</button>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with an adverb from the box: <b>luckily &middot; unfortunately &middot; remarkably</b>. Use each one once.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">10</span><span class=\"body\"><input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"luckily\" data-why=\"<b>Luckily</b> introduces good news that came by chance.\"> , he had a bottle of water in his bag.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">11</span><span class=\"body\"><input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"unfortunately\" data-why=\"<b>Unfortunately</b> introduces bad news.\"> , the phone had stopped working two hours earlier.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">12</span><span class=\"body\">The ring was in the soil for ten years and, <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"remarkably\" data-why=\"<b>Remarkably</b> = surprisingly, almost unbelievably.\"> , it still fits her.</span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 2 · GRAMMAR ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 2 &middot; Grammar &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 13&ndash;26</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">13</span><span class=\"body\">While he&hellip; for the path, he fell into a stream.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">looked</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">had looked</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">was looking</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">14</span><span class=\"body\">His phone did not work because he&hellip; it in the water.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">was dropping</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">had dropped</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">has dropped</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">15</span><span class=\"body\">He&hellip; not to take the cable car with his friends.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">decided</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">was deciding</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">had been deciding</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">16</span><span class=\"body\">By the time the balloon landed, millions of people&hellip; it on television.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">watched</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">have watched</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">were watching</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the verb in brackets into the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">17</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>bake</i>) She <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"had been baking\" data-why=\"An activity going on before the key moment &rarr; past perfect continuous.\"> all morning when she noticed the ring was gone.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">18</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>interview</i>) While reporters <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"were interviewing\" data-why=\"Background action in progress &rarr; past continuous.\"> the family, the boy mentioned the show.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">19</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>find</i>) People <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"found\" data-why=\"A single completed event &rarr; past simple.\"> him twenty-four days later.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">20</span><span class=\"body\">(<i>already / eat</i>) By the time we arrived, they <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"had already eaten\" data-why=\"Earlier than another past point &rarr; past perfect, with <i>already</i> inside it.\"> .</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the linker that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">21</span><span class=\"body\">He waited in the stream&hellip; somebody finally found him.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">as soon as</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">until</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">by the time</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">22</span><span class=\"body\">&hellip; the interview ended, the police reopened the case.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">As soon as</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">Until</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">While</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete each sentence with the correct form.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">23</span><span class=\"body\">While I <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"was walking\" data-why=\"Two past actions at the same time: the long one takes the past continuous &mdash; <i>was walking</i>.\"> home, I saw him.</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">24</span><span class=\"body\">When we arrived, they <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"had left\" data-why=\"The earlier of two past events takes the past perfect &mdash; <i>had left</i>.\"> an hour before.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Write the second sentence so that it means the same as the first.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">25</span><span class=\"body\">First he broke his leg. Then he realized his phone was wet.<br>By the time he realized his phone was wet, he <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"had broken his leg|had already broken his leg\" data-why=\"The earlier event &rarr; past perfect.\"></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">26</span><span class=\"body\">The film finished. Immediately after that, she phoned me.<br>She phoned me <input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"as soon as the film finished|as soon as the film had finished\" data-why=\"<b>As soon as</b> = immediately after.\"></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 3 · READING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 3 &middot; Reading &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 27&ndash;34</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the whole text once before you answer anything.</p>\n\n      <article class=\"reading\">\n        <h3>The island that was not there</h3>\n        <p class=\"stand\">For more than a century, a small island appeared on maps of the Pacific. In 2012 a ship sailed to the spot and found nothing at all.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">A</span>Sandy Island sat in the Coral Sea, between Australia and New Caledonia, a long thin shape about twenty-four kilometres from north to south. It had been on charts since 1876, when a British whaling ship reported passing it. Later it appeared on French maps, then on scientific databases, and finally on the world&rsquo;s most-used online map. Nobody had checked it, because nobody had needed to.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">B</span>In November 2012 an Australian research ship was crossing the area on its way to somewhere else. The scientists on board noticed that their own instruments disagreed with the map: while the chart showed land, the equipment was reporting more than a kilometre of water. They changed course to look. When they reached the position, there was nothing there &mdash; only ocean, in every direction.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">C</span>The team announced what they had found, and the story circulated within hours. Newspapers called it the island that had been un-discovered. Map companies removed it quietly. But the interesting question was never whether the island existed; it was why nobody had asked for a hundred and thirty-six years.</p>\n        <p><span class=\"pmark\">D</span>The answer, historians of cartography say, is that maps copy each other. A whaling captain in 1876 wrote down something he believed he had seen. The next map-maker did not sail to the Coral Sea; he copied the previous chart, because that is what map-makers do. By the time computers arrived, the mistake had been repeated so often that it looked like evidence. As soon as one modern ship bothered to sail there, it took twenty minutes to disprove.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">27</span><span class=\"body\">The main point of the text is that\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">online maps are less reliable than paper ones</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">the Coral Sea has never been properly explored</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">an error can survive for a long time simply by being copied</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">28</span><span class=\"body\">Why did the scientists change course in 2012?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">they had been sent to find the island</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">their instruments did not agree with the chart</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">a newspaper had asked them to check it</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">True, False, or Not given? Choose for each sentence.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">29</span><span class=\"body\">The island first appeared on a chart in 1876. <select data-answer=\"T\" data-why=\"Paragraph A: it had been on charts since <b>1876</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">30</span><span class=\"body\">The research ship had set out specially to investigate the island. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph B: it was crossing the area <b>on its way to somewhere else</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"F\">False</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">31</span><span class=\"body\">The whaling captain invented the island deliberately. <select data-answer=\"N\" data-why=\"Paragraph D says he <i>believed he had seen</i> something. The text never accuses him.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option><option value=\"F\">False</option></select></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">32</span><span class=\"body\">Map companies argued publicly about removing the island. <select data-answer=\"F\" data-why=\"Paragraph C: they removed it <b>quietly</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option value=\"F\">False</option><option value=\"T\">True</option><option value=\"N\">Not given</option></select></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Answer the last two questions about the whole text.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">33</span><span class=\"body\">In paragraph D, <i>it looked like evidence</i> means that the repeated error\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">seemed to prove itself because so many maps agreed</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">had been tested by several ships</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">was written down in a scientific paper</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">34</span><span class=\"body\">Which sentence best describes the writer&rsquo;s attitude to the map-makers?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">They were dishonest and should be blamed.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">They behaved normally for their profession, and that is the problem.</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">They were far more careful than modern scientists.</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 4 · LISTENING ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 4 &middot; Listening &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 35&ndash;40</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Read the questions first. Then play each recording twice.</p>\n\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('story',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Recording 1 &middot; the story on the mountain\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 2.1</b>Original coursebook recording</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Recording 1. Complete the notes with one word or a number.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">35</span><span class=\"body\">He had eaten at a restaurant on top of the <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"mountain\" data-why=\"He had been at a barbecue restaurant on top of the <b>mountain</b>.\"> .</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">36</span><span class=\"body\">He was found <input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"24|twenty-four|twenty four\" data-why=\"It was <b>twenty-four</b> days before they found him.\"> days later.</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Recording 1. Choose the best answer.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">37</span><span class=\"body\">What kept him alive?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">water mixed with barbecue sauce</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">food he had taken from the restaurant</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">supplies dropped by a helicopter</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">38</span><span class=\"body\">Why were teams of people out searching the mountain?\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">they were walking the same path by chance</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">the restaurant had closed and they were going home</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">somebody had realized he was missing</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <div class=\"player\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('n3',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Recording 2 &middot; sentence about the balloon\n        </button>\n        <button class=\"btn btn-audio\" onclick=\"playClip('n5',this,'Stop')\">\n          <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M8 5v14l11-7z\"/></svg> Recording 3 &middot; sentence about the interview\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"wave\"></div>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><b>Navigate B1+ &middot; Audio 2.4</b>Two single sentences</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Listen and write the linking word you hear.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">39</span><span class=\"body\">Recording 2: &ldquo;<input class=\"gap gap-lg\" data-answer=\"by the time\" data-why=\"The sentence begins <b>By the time</b> the balloon landed&hellip;\"> the balloon landed&hellip;&rdquo;</span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">40</span><span class=\"body\">Recording 3: &ldquo;&hellip;<input class=\"gap\" data-answer=\"while\" data-why=\"<b>While</b> reporters were interviewing the family&hellip;\"> reporters were interviewing the family&hellip;&rdquo;</span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 5 · FUNCTIONAL LANGUAGE ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 5 &middot; Functional language &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 41&ndash;48</span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">What would you say? Choose the phrase that fits.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">41</span><span class=\"body\">You want to start a story so that nobody interrupts you.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"b\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">In the end&hellip;</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">You&rsquo;ll never believe what happened&hellip;</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">What happened next?</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">42</span><span class=\"body\">You are the listener, and you want the teller to carry on.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"c\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">Anyway, that&rsquo;s why&hellip;</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">And suddenly&hellip;</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">Go on &mdash; what happened next?</button></div></span></div>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">43</span><span class=\"body\">You want to signal that the surprise is one sentence away.\n        <div class=\"opts\" data-correct=\"a\"><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"a\">You&rsquo;re not going to believe this, but&hellip;</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"b\">It turned out that&hellip;</button><button class=\"opt\" data-val=\"c\">That reminds me of&hellip;</button></div></span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Who says each phrase &mdash; the person telling the story, or the person listening?</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">44&ndash;47</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"sortbox\">\n          <div class=\"sortpool\"><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Teller\">So then&hellip;</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Listener\">No way! That&rsquo;s incredible!</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Teller\">In the end, it turned out that&hellip;</button><button class=\"swd\" data-col=\"Listener\">Oh no, that&rsquo;s awful.</button></div>\n          <div class=\"sortcols\"><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Teller\"><h5>The teller</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div><div class=\"sortcol\" data-col=\"Listener\"><h5>The listener</h5><div class=\"drop\"></div></div></div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <p class=\"subline\">Put the four parts of the spoken story in order.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"num\">48</span><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"order\" data-order=\"s3,s1,s4,s2\">\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"s1\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">So I was walking home at about ten when I heard something behind me.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"s2\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">Anyway, that&rsquo;s why I never take that road at night now.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"s3\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">I&rsquo;ll never forget the night I lost my keys.</span></button>\n          <button class=\"ochip\" data-val=\"s4\"><span class=\"pin\"></span><span class=\"txt\">You&rsquo;re not going to believe this, but it was my own cat.</span></button>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <!-- ============ PART 6 · PUTTING IT TOGETHER ============ -->\n      <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 6 &middot; Putting it together &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">questions 49&ndash;54</span></div>\n      <p class=\"subline\">Complete the conversation. Every gap tests something from a different lesson in this unit.</p>\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <div class=\"chat\">\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b><select data-answer=\"You&rsquo;ll never believe what happened\" data-why=\"A story opener that claims the floor.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>In the end, it turned out</option><option>You&rsquo;ll never believe what happened</option><option>What happened next</option></select> to me on Saturday.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Timur</b>Go on.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>I <select data-answer=\"was queuing\" data-why=\"A long background action &rarr; past continuous.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>queued</option><option>had queued</option><option>was queuing</option></select> outside the shop at six in the morning &mdash; half-price day.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Timur</b>Of course you were.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b><select data-answer=\"As soon as\" data-why=\"Immediately after &rarr; <b>as soon as</b>.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>Until</option><option>As soon as</option><option>By the time</option></select> the doors opened, everybody ran. And <select data-answer=\"suddenly\" data-why=\"Marks the turning point in a spoken story.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>finally</option><option>suddenly</option><option>personally</option></select> somebody knocked into me and I dropped my phone.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg\"><b>Timur</b>Oh no, that&rsquo;s awful.</div>\n          <div class=\"msg you\"><b>You</b>It gets worse. By the time I found it, three people <select data-answer=\"had walked\" data-why=\"Earlier than the moment of finding it &rarr; past perfect.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>walked</option><option>were walking</option><option>had walked</option></select> over it. <select data-answer=\"Luckily,\" data-why=\"Introduces the good news that came by chance.\"><option value=\"\">&mdash;</option><option>Unfortunately,</option><option>Luckily,</option><option>Personally,</option></select> the screen was fine.</div>\n        </div>\n      </span></div>\n\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" onclick=\"checkReview(this)\" style=\"margin-top:24px\">Check my answers</button>\n      <div class=\"res\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div id=\"reviewResult\" class=\"review-result\"></div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 7 · WRITING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Part 7 &middot; Writing &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">Write 100&ndash;120 words. Give yourself twenty minutes.</p>\n    <div class=\"opentask\" data-open data-tid=\"test-write\">\n      <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"body\">\n        <p class=\"ohint\"><b>The task.</b> Write the story of something that went wrong and turned out well &mdash; yours, or somebody else&rsquo;s. Open with one line that promises a story. Set an ordinary scene. Say what everybody did about it. Signal the surprise one sentence before it lands. Finish with where things stand today.</p>\n        <textarea placeholder=\"I&rsquo;ll never forget the day&hellip;   It was an ordinary&hellip;   While we were&hellip;   You&rsquo;re not going to believe this, but&hellip;   Remarkably,&hellip;\" data-track></textarea>\n      </span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"bubble useful\">\n      <div class=\"blab\">Your story must contain</div>\n      <ul>\n        <li>one <b>past continuous</b> for the scene, and one <b>past perfect</b> for something earlier</li>\n        <li>two different linkers from <b>when &middot; while &middot; as soon as &middot; by the time &middot; until</b></li>\n        <li>one comment adverb: <b>luckily, unfortunately, remarkably, curiously</b></li>\n        <li>the line that warns the reader the surprise is coming</li>\n        <li>four words from this unit</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ============ PART 8 · SPEAKING ============ -->\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">Part 8 &middot; Speaking &nbsp;<span class=\"qcount\">assessed against the criteria</span></div>\n    <div class=\"opentask speak\" data-open data-tid=\"test-speak\">\n      <div class=\"sp-head\"><span class=\"sp-ic\">&#127908;</span>\n        <div><b>Speaking &mdash; tell it, do not read it</b><span>Extended turn</span></div></div>\n      <p class=\"sp-task\"><b>Part A.</b> Tell the same story out loud, without reading what you wrote. Ninety seconds. <b>Part B.</b> Then answer: <i>why do false stories travel so fast?</i> Give your opinion and one reason.</p>\n      <ul class=\"sp-list\">\n        <li>an opener that claims the floor, before the first event</li>\n        <li>a scene set in the past continuous</li>\n        <li>at least two sequencers as the story moves</li>\n        <li>the warning line before the surprise, and a closing line that hands the floor back</li>\n      </ul>\n      <div class=\"sp-lang\"><b>Use this language</b>I&rsquo;ll never forget the day&hellip; &middot; So I was &hellip;ing when&hellip; &middot; So then&hellip; &middot; The next thing I knew&hellip; &middot; You&rsquo;re not going to believe this, but&hellip; &middot; Anyway, that&rsquo;s why&hellip;</div>\n      <div class=\"rec\">\n        <div class=\"rec-row\">\n          <button class=\"rec-btn\" type=\"button\" onclick=\"recToggle(this)\" aria-label=\"Record your answer\" title=\"Record\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M12 14a3 3 0 0 0 3-3V6a3 3 0 0 0-6 0v5a3 3 0 0 0 3 3zm5-3a5 5 0 0 1-10 0H5a7 7 0 0 0 6 6.9V21h2v-3.1A7 7 0 0 0 19 11z\"/></svg></button>\n          <div class=\"rec-label\"><b>Record your answer</b><span>Press the microphone and speak</span></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-wave\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>\n          <div class=\"rec-time\">0:00</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"rec-takes\"></div>\n        <div class=\"rec-note\">Record it, play it back, then submit it for assessment.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"instruction\" style=\"margin-top:30px\">Parts 7 and 8 &middot; Assessment</div>\n    <p class=\"subline\">These two parts are not marked automatically and they are not marked by you. Submit your writing and record your speaking, then your teacher &mdash; or the AI tutor &mdash; scores each part against the criteria below and writes the feedback.</p>\n    <div class=\"rubric-slot\">\n      <ul class=\"reqlist\">\n        <li>my story has an opening line that promises a story and then stops</li>\n        <li>the ordinary scene comes before the strange part</li>\n        <li>I used a past continuous for the scene and a past perfect for something earlier</li>\n        <li>I used two different time linkers correctly</li>\n        <li>I warned the reader one sentence before the surprise</li>\n        <li>I told the story out loud without reading it</li>\n        <li>I used at least two sequencers while speaking</li>\n        <li>I closed the spoken story instead of just stopping</li>\n      </ul>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n"}